# Builds read these keys only from the shell environment, never from .env. A release build sets
# APTABASE_APP_KEY, SENTRY_DSN and FEATURE_ELIGIBILITY_URL in the release job environment.
# A shell-wide export would reach later dev and E2E builds. Leave APTABASE_HOST unset
# unless the key is a self-hosted (A-SH-*) or development (A-DEV-*) one. Only Jest loads .env, through
# its dotenv setup, so a value put there reaches tests and never a bundle.

# Aptabase app key for usage telemetry, from the Aptabase dashboard
# (Settings → Instructions). The key's region picks the host on its own:
# A-EU-* → https://eu.aptabase.com, A-US-* → https://us.aptabase.com.
# Empty disables usage telemetry entirely, whatever the in-app setting says.
APTABASE_APP_KEY=
# Aptabase host, needed ONLY for a self-hosted (A-SH-*) or development (A-DEV-*)
# key, which have no region to derive a host from. An origin, not a full URL -
# the /api/v0/event path is added for you. Setting it also overrides the region
# default for an A-EU-*/A-US-* key, for a staging proxy.
APTABASE_HOST=
# Sentry EU DSN for crash reports. Empty disables reporting entirely.
SENTRY_DSN=
# Public feature eligibility URL, ending /v1/eligibility. Empty keeps configured
# place restrictions closed. MaxMind credentials belong only to the server.
FEATURE_ELIGIBILITY_URL=
